Description: Computes chlorophyll a fluorescence transient (OJIP)
    parameters of the JIP-test from fluorescence summary data, including
    minimum and maximum fluorescence, selected transient steps, and area.
    Provides quantum yields, specific fluxes per reaction center,
    phenomenological fluxes per cross section, and the performance index.
    Converts exported fluorescence traces into summary values with
    documented, instrument-specific time targets, tolerance windows,
    background handling, and quality flags, with presets for traces
    exported by 'Biolyzer' (Handy-PEA data) and by the 'FluorPen' software.
    Includes validation functions that compare results with parameters
    exported by these programs, visualization tools, and an interactive
    'shiny' interface. The implemented calculations are based on Strasser
    et al. (2004) <doi:10.1007/978-1-4020-3218-9_12> and Tsimilli-Michael
    (2020) <doi:10.32615/ps.2019.150>.
